{"key":"nc","num":"215","title":"New Caledonia","blurb":"Every place GeoNames records above 500 people in New Caledonia: 63 towns and villages, grouped by region and ordered by population.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Caledonia","d":"New Caledonia is a French territory consisting of a group of islands in the southwest Pacific Ocean, 220 km (140 mi) southwest of Vanuatu and 1,210 km (750 mi) east of Australia. Located 16,100 km (10,000 mi) from Metropolitan France, it forms a sui generis collectivity of the French Republic, having a unique legal status enshrined in a dedicated chapter of the French Constitution.\nThe archipelago, part of the Melanesia subregion, includes the main island of Grande Terre, the Loyalty Islands, the Chesterfield Islands, the Belep archipelago, the Isle of Pines, and a few remote islets. The Chesterfield Islands are in the Coral Sea. French people, especially locals, call Grande Terre le Caillou, a nickname also used more generally for New Caledonia itself. Pro-independence Kanak parties use the name (la) Kanaky to refer to New Caledonia, a term coined in the 1980s from the ethnic name of the indigenous Melanesian Kanak people, who make up 41% of New Caledonia's population. New Caledonia is associated with the European Union as an overseas country and territory (OCT).\nNew Caledonia has a land area of 18,575 km2 (7,172 sq mi) divided into three provinces. The North and South Provinces are on the New Caledonian mainland, while the Loyalty Islands Province is a series of four inhabited islands off the east coast of mainland (from north to south: Ouvéa, Lifou, Tiga, and Maré). New Caledonia's population of 264,596 (April 2025 census) is of diverse origins and varies by geography; in the North and Loyalty Islands Provinces, the indigenous Kanaks predominate, while the wealthy South Province contains significant populations of European (Caldoches and Metropolitan French), Kanak, and Polynesian (mostly Wallisian) origin, as well as smaller groups of Southeast Asian, Pied-Noir, and North African heritage. The capital of New Caledonia is Nouméa.","groups":[{"name":"South Province","items":[{"n":"Nouméa","u":"https://www.geonames.org/2139521","p":93060,"t":"capital"},{"n":"Mont-Dore","u":"https://www.geonames.org/2140066","p":24680,"t":"town"},{"n":"Dumbéa","u":"https://www.geonames.org/2141394","p":19346,"t":"town"},{"n":"Païta","u":"https://www.geonames.org/2138981","p":12617,"t":"town"},{"n":"Vallée des Colons","u":"https://www.geonames.org/11956197","p":8866,"t":"village"},{"n":"Magenta","u":"https://www.geonames.org/11956106","p":7169,"t":"village"},{"n":"Rivière-Salée","u":"https://www.geonames.org/11956101","p":6873,"t":"village"},{"n":"Bourail","u":"https://www.geonames.org/2141714","p":5531,"t":"village"},{"n":"Portes de Fer","u":"https://www.geonames.org/11185984","p":4093,"t":"village"},{"n":"Aérodrome","u":"https://www.geonames.org/13526992","p":3951,"t":"village"},{"n":"Septième Kilomètre","u":"https://www.geonames.org/11956196","p":3944,"t":"village"},{"n":"Anse-Vata","u":"https://www.geonames.org/10861676","p":3729,"t":"village"},{"n":"Val Plaisance","u":"https://www.geonames.org/11956109","p":3631,"t":"village"},{"n":"N'Géa","u":"https://www.geonames.org/10861677","p":3624,"t":"village"},{"n":"Nouville","u":"https://www.geonames.org/2139508","p":3481,"t":"village"},{"n":"Normandie","u":"https://www.geonames.org/2139544","p":3316,"t":"village"},{"n":"Kaméré","u":"https://www.geonames.org/11185986","p":3127,"t":"village"},{"n":"Sixième Kilomètre","u":"https://www.geonames.org/11956194","p":2949,"t":"village"},{"n":"La Foa","u":"https://www.geonames.org/2140466","p":2947,"t":"village"},{"n":"Trianon","u":"https://www.geonames.org/11956110","p":2944,"t":"village"},{"n":"Thio","u":"https://www.geonames.org/2138103","p":2748,"t":"village"},{"n":"Faubourg Blanchot","u":"https://www.geonames.org/2141894","p":2730,"t":"village"},{"n":"Vallée du Génie","u":"https://www.geonames.org/11956114",